---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Practice — Ruijie Wu" description="Psychotherapy and embodied approaches with Ruijie Wu.">
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Practice</span>
    <h1>Making room<br /><em>for experience.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Therapeutic work is not about becoming someone else. It can be a process of meeting more of who you are, with attention, honesty and care.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Individual psychotherapy</h3><p>Exploring emotional difficulties, relationships, identity, grief, transitions and questions of meaning.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Embodied exploration</h3><p>Bringing attention to sensation, posture, gesture, movement and the felt dimensions of experience.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Trauma-informed work</h3><p>Working with sensitivity to safety, pacing, choice and the many ways people adapt to overwhelming experience.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <h2>How I understand the work</h2>
      <p>I am interested in a collaborative relationship in which your experience is taken seriously and does not need to fit a predetermined explanation. We may work with words, images, bodily awareness or movement, depending on your wishes and what feels appropriate.</p>
      <p>My approach is shaped by existential-humanistic therapy, feminist perspectives, psychomotor practice and ongoing learning in dance movement therapy.</p>
      <h3>Enquiries</h3>
      <p>If you would like to ask about current availability, format or fees, please get in touch. We can clarify whether the work I offer is suitable for what you are looking for.</p>
      <p><em>This website is not an emergency service. If you are in immediate danger or need urgent support, please contact local emergency or crisis services.</em></p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>Get in touch <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
